        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114303,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA05.0 Developmental odontogenic cysts</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114304,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Acceptable:</em> in infants: gingival cyst of the newborn, Bohn nodules; in adults: gingival cyst of adult.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Bohn nodules (in adults); alveolar cysts.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:33:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114305,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114306,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In adults, most cysts arise in the gingiva of the mandibular premolar/canine region {26233969; 29156092} or (less frequently) in the anterior maxillary gingiva, almost always on the buccal aspect of the alveolus. In infants, the cysts occur anywhere on the edentulous alveolar ridge of the mandible or maxilla {6172766; 4506677}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114307,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p >Gingival cyst of the adult (GCA) usually forms a single painless, well-circumscribed nodule of the attached gingivae, sometimes with a bluish-grey translucent appearance. Radiographs are not helpful in detecting GCA, despite occasional superficial erosion of the underlying alveolar bone. Gingival cyst of the infant (GCI) presents as small (&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mm) white nodules on the alveolar mucosa, which are often multiple {14155470}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T16:49:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114308,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GCA accounts for &lt;&nbsp;0.5% of odontogenic cysts {30758760}. The majority of patients are in their fifth or sixth decade of life {12146543; 29156092; 30758760}. GCI is found in as many as 90% of neonates but is rare after the age of 3&nbsp;months {6679627}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114309,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 128,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114310,
